@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "provisioning.security"

Feature:  Koroneiki to Provisioning Product Admin Permissions
	Testing to assure that provisioning product admin permissions works properly.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails
	* I create a provisioning user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | provisioning.admin                    |
	| Email Address | provisioning.admin@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Provisioning                          |
	| Last Name     | Admin                                 |
	* I assign the provisioning user with the email address "provisioning.admin@liferay.com.broken" to the provisioning role "Provisioning Admin"

Teardown:
	* I tear down the products on koroneiki with the following names
	| A Visible DXP Product    |
	| A Visible Portal Product |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from provisioning
	| provisioning.admin@liferay.com.broken |

Scenario: Create products
	Testing the ability to create products in the provisioning product index 

	Given I log into the provisioning homepage as "provisioning.admin@liferay.com.broken" with password "${staticProvisioningQaUserPassword}"
	And I update my password upon login to "test"
	And I go to the product index page
	And I click on the new product button
	And I populate and save the product form with the following values
	| Name | Input  | A Visible Portal Product |
	| Type | Select | Primary                  |
	And I search the products page using the keyword "A"
	Then I should be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "A Visible Portal Product" and the following values
	| Name | A Visible Portal Product |
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "A Visible Portal Product" and the following values
	| Name                    | A Visible Portal Product |         |
	| Product Field and Value | type                     | primary |

Scenario: Update products
	Testing the ability to update products in the provisioning product index 

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Visible DXP Product | |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "provisioning.admin@liferay.com.broken" with password "${staticProvisioningQaUserPassword}"
	And I update my password upon login to "test"
	And I go to the product index page
	And I search the products page using the keyword "A"
	And I click on the product with the name "A Visible DXP Product" on the provisioning index
	And I populate and save the product form with the following values
	| Name | Input  | A Visible Portal Product |
	| Type | Select | Primary                  |
	And I search the products page using the keyword "A"
	Then I should be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "A Visible Portal Product" and the following values
	| Name | A Visible Portal Product |
	And I should not be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "A Visible DXP Product"
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "A Visible Portal Product" and the following values
	| Name                    | A Visible Portal Product |         |
	| Product Field and Value | type                     | primary |

Scenario: Delete products
	Testing the ability to update products in the provisioning product index 

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Visible DXP Product | |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "provisioning.admin@liferay.com.broken" with password "${staticProvisioningQaUserPassword}"
	And I update my password upon login to "test"
	And I go to the product index page
	And I search the products page using the keyword "A"
	And I click on the delete button for the product "A Visible DXP Product"
	And I search the products page using the keyword "A"
	Then I should not be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "A Visible DXP Product"
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "A Visible DXP Product"